  "body": "# cuprated 0.1.0-preview Kesterite\r\nCuprate is a modular Monero node written in Rust. To get started, see: <https://user.cuprate.org>.\r\n\r\n**This is a preview release for beta. It includes initial wallet support.**\r\n\r\nThis release contains updates to our RPC interface to allow wallets to connect to Cuprate. Wallets can now sync the blockchain\r\nand send transactions with Cuprate.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n- Initial wallet RPC support ([#624](https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/pull/624), [#631](https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/pull/631), [#634](https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/pull/634), [#636](https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/pull/636), [#637](https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/pull/637), [#641](https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/pull/641), [#647](https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/pull/647), [#653](https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/pull/653), [#654](https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/pull/654))\r\n- Add offline mode ([#656](https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/pull/656))\r\n- Add graceful shutdown ([#585](https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/pull/585))\r\n- Add embeddable `Node::launch()` library ([#592](https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/pull/592))\r\n- Add regtest and fakechain support ([#607](https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/pull/607))\r\n- Improve Tor networking ([#640](https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/pull/640))\r\n- Support SOCKS5 proxy URLs ([#596](https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/pull/596))\r\n- Add custom allocator options ([#658](https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/pull/658))\r\n- Add Docker, Alpine, FreeBSD, and OpenBSD support ([#659](https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/pull/659))\r\n- Respect `NO_COLOR` and non-interactive terminals ([#618](https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/pull/618))\r\n- Fix the `--network` argument ([#649](https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/pull/649))\r\n- Remove RPC payment support ([#646](https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/pull/646))\r\n\r\n## Downloads\r\nFor convenience, the following binaries are produced using GitHub CI in a non-reproducible way; it is highly recommended to build `cuprated` from source instead, see <https://user.cuprate.org/getting-started/source>.\r\n\r\n| OS      | Architecture | Download |\r\n|---------|--------------|----------|\r\n| Windows | x64          | <https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/releases/download/cuprated-0.1.0-preview/cuprated-0.1.0-preview-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip>\r\n| macOS   | ARM64        | <https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/releases/download/cuprated-0.1.0-preview/cuprated-0.1.0-preview-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz>\r\n| Linux   | x64          | <https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/releases/download/cuprated-0.1.0-preview/cuprated-0.1.0-preview-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz>\r\n| Linux   | ARM64        | <https://github.com/Cuprate/cuprate/releases/download/cuprated-0.1.0-preview/cuprated-0.1.0-preview-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz>\r\n\r\n## Contributors\r\nThank you to everyone who directly contributed to this release:\r\n\r\n- @Boog900\r\n- @jpk68\r\n- @redsh4de\r\n- @SyntheticBird45\r\n\r\nThere are other contributors that are not listed here, thank you to them as well.\r\n",
